.SH DESCRIPTION
Test that two backends can share the same NVMe controller
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B
\fBxnvme-test-dual-be-io-cmp\fP(1)
Write a known pattern to LBA 0 through the \fB--be\fP backend, read it back
through the \fB--alt-be\fP backend, and verify the data matches.
Both backends share the same NVMe controller on the same device URI.
NOTE: overwrites LBA 0; only use on a device where that is safe.
.PP
.nf
.fam C
  xnvme-test-dual-be-idfy-cmp(1)  Issue an Identify Controller command through each of the two backends
.fam T
.fi
sharing the same NVMe controller, then byte-compare the responses.
A mismatch indicates dual-backend operation returned inconsistent data.
.RE
.PP

